{"title":"Career Roadmap · Design Researcher","role":"Design Researcher","summary":"A Design Researcher studies people, their behaviours, needs, motivations, environments and problems to help organisations create better products, services and experiences.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Product / Industrial Design"},"about":[{"label":"Degree–Career Alignment","text":"Excellent"},{"label":"Career Type","text":"Research + Design + Human Behaviour + Product Strategy"},{"label":"Typical Entry Level","text":"Design Research Intern / Research Assistant / Junior Design Researcher / UX Research Associate"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"What Does a Design Researcher Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Design Researcher studies people, their behaviours, needs, motivations, environments and problems to help organisations create better products, services and experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"In product/industrial design, the researcher may investigate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How people currently use a product"},{"text":"Unmet customer needs"},{"text":"User frustrations and pain points"},{"text":"Product usability and ergonomics"},{"text":"Market and competitor behaviour"},{"text":"Cultural and behavioural trends"},{"text":"Materials, manufacturing and product-use contexts"},{"text":"User reactions to prototypes"},{"text":"Why a product succeeds or fails"},{"text":"Opportunities for new product development"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits between research, design, psychology, business and product development."},{"type":"note","label":"Important positioning","text":"“Design Researcher” is a broad title. A B.Des graduate can enter through junior design research, UX research, user research, product research or design strategy roles and specialise over time."}]},{"heading":"Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"During B.Des"},{"text":"Design Research Intern, UX Research Intern, Product Research Intern"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Design Researcher, Design Research Assistant, UX Research Associate, User Research Associate"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Design Researcher, UX Researcher, Product Researcher, Consumer Researcher"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Design Researcher, Senior UX Researcher, Lead Researcher"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Design Research Lead, Research Manager, Head of Design Research, Design Strategy Lead"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Service Design Researcher, Product Researcher, Behavioural Researcher, Consumer Insights Researcher, Design Strategist"}]]}]},{"heading":"Core Work of a Design Researcher","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A typical research project can follow this process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Business/Product Question","Research Plan","User Recruitment","Field Research","Interviews/Observation","Data Analysis","Insights","Opportunity Areas","Design Recommendations","Prototype Testing","Validation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Common research activities"},{"type":"table","header":["Research Area","Activities"],"rows":[[{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Interviews, surveys, observation"}],[{"text":"Contextual research"},{"text":"Field visits, contextual inquiry, diary studies"}],[{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"Usability testing, task analysis"}],[{"text":"Product research"},{"text":"Product-use studies, prototype evaluation"}],[{"text":"Behavioural research"},{"text":"Motivation, habits, decision-making"}],[{"text":"Market research"},{"text":"Competitor and category analysis"}],[{"text":"Ethnographic research"},{"text":"Studying users in real environments"}],[{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Surveys, experiments, analytics"}],[{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Interviews, focus groups, thematic analysis"}],[{"text":"Design synthesis"},{"text":"Affinity mapping, journey maps, personas"}],[{"text":"Product strategy"},{"text":"Opportunity identification and prioritisation"}]]}]},{"heading":"Skills to Build During B.Des","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design & Research Foundations"},{"type":"flow","items":["Focus on understanding people","design","observation."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Design foundations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design thinking"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Form and function"},{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Product observation"},{"text":"Basic ergonomics"},{"text":"Human-centred design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research foundations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Interviewing"},{"text":"Note-taking"},{"text":"Problem identification"},{"text":"Basic qualitative research"},{"text":"User personas"},{"text":"Journey mapping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Adobe Photoshop"},{"text":"Google Forms"},{"text":"Excel/Google Sheets"}]},{"type":"h","text":"First project"},{"type":"h","text":"Everyday Product Behaviour Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose something such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Water bottle"},{"text":"Backpack"},{"text":"Office chair"},{"text":"Kitchen appliance"},{"text":"Mobile phone"},{"text":"School bag"},{"text":"Public transport ticketing system"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Observe 15–20 users and document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"How they use it"},{"text":"Problems encountered"},{"text":"Workarounds"},{"text":"Emotional reactions"},{"text":"Improvement opportunities"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Research Methods + Human Behaviour","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Move beyond simply observing users."},{"type":"h","text":"Research methods"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Semi-structured interviews"},{"text":"Contextual inquiry"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"Card sorting"},{"text":"Concept testing"},{"text":"Comparative research"},{"text":"Competitive analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn basic statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"You do not need to become a statistician, but understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Distribution"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Basic hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Survey bias"},{"text":"Research validity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful topics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural psychology"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Human perception"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Memory"},{"text":"Behavioural economics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"h","text":"User Research for a Consumer Product"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Research why college students struggle to organise their study materials."},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"15 interviews"},{"text":"100+ survey responses"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Competitor research"},{"text":"User journey mapping"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then produce:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Insights","Opportunities","Product recommendations"]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Professional Design Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is where the student should start becoming employer-ready."},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced qualitative research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Thematic analysis"},{"text":"Coding interview data"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"Behavioural segmentation"},{"text":"Persona development"},{"text":"Journey mapping"},{"text":"Experience mapping"},{"text":"Jobs-to-be-Done"},{"text":"Opportunity mapping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Cross-tabulation"},{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression basics"},{"text":"A/B testing fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research tools"},{"type":"table","header":["Tool","Purpose"],"rows":[[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Prototypes and research artefacts"}],[{"text":"FigJam/Miro"},{"text":"Research synthesis"}],[{"text":"Qualtrics/Google Forms"},{"text":"Surveys"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Data analysis"}],[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Research dashboards"}],[{"text":"SPSS/R"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"}],[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Advanced research/data analysis"}],[{"text":"Dovetail/qualitative research platforms"},{"text":"Interview/research analysis"}],[{"text":"Notion/Airtable"},{"text":"Research repositories"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"AI-assisted research"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how AI can assist with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Research-note organisation"},{"text":"Initial thematic coding"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Competitor research"},{"text":"Pattern detection"},{"text":"Research repository search"},{"text":"Research synthesis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But never treat AI-generated interpretations as validated research findings."}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Specialisation + Industry Portfolio","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Choose one primary research direction."},{"type":"h","text":"Track A — Product Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Consumer products"},{"text":"Product usability"},{"text":"Product adoption"},{"text":"Product-market fit"},{"text":"Product testing"},{"text":"Customer needs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track B — UX Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital products"},{"text":"Apps"},{"text":"Websites"},{"text":"Usability"},{"text":"User behaviour"},{"text":"Interaction research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track C — Industrial Design Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical products"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Manufacturing context"},{"text":"Product usage"},{"text":"Human-product interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track D — Service Design Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Customer journeys"},{"text":"Service systems"},{"text":"Touchpoints"},{"text":"Frontstage/backstage processes"},{"text":"Service blueprints"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track E — Consumer & Market Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Brand perception"},{"text":"Market segmentation"},{"text":"Category research"},{"text":"Trend research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Track F — Behavioural Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human behaviour"},{"text":"Psychology"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Behavioural economics"},{"text":"Experimental research"}]}]},{"heading":"Four-Year Development Plan","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Main Focus","Output"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design + observation"},{"text":"2–3 mini research projects"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Interviews + surveys + usability"},{"text":"2 substantial research projects"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Qualitative + quantitative research"},{"text":"2–3 industry-style case studies"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Specialisation + internship"},{"text":"Professional research portfolio"}],[{"text":"Graduation"},{"text":"Job readiness"},{"text":"4–6 excellent research case studies"}]]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Is Extremely Important","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For Design Research, a portfolio should not simply show attractive designs."},{"type":"p","text":"It should demonstrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research question","Method","Evidence","Analysis","Insight","Design implication"]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Build 4–6 strong case studies."},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 1 — Product Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Research an existing physical product."},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research objective"},{"text":"Research questions"},{"text":"Participants"},{"text":"Method"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Findings"},{"text":"Affinity map"},{"text":"User journey"},{"text":"Key insights"},{"text":"Opportunities"},{"text":"Product recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 2 — Usability Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Test an existing product/interface."},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tasks"},{"text":"Participants"},{"text":"Usability problems"},{"text":"Severity"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Recommendations"},{"text":"Retest results"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 3 — Consumer Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study a product category."},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"Why are young consumers choosing reusable water bottles?"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Consumer motivations"},{"text":"Price"},{"text":"Brand"},{"text":"Sustainability"},{"text":"Design"},{"text":"Convenience"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 4 — Ethnographic Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study behaviour in a real environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public transport"},{"text":"College cafeteria"},{"text":"Hospital waiting area"},{"text":"Retail store"},{"text":"Airport"},{"text":"Gym"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 5 — Product Innovation"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify an unmet need and conduct:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Opportunity","Concept","Prototype","User Testing"]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study 6 — Data-Driven Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Survey","statistics","dashboard","qualitative insights"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates modern research capability."}]},{"heading":"Research Methods Employers Expect","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Method","Importance"],"rows":[[{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Survey research"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Contextual inquiry"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Competitive research"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Ethnographic research"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Diary studies"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Concept testing"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Quantitative analysis"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Behavioural experiments"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Trend research"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}]]}]},{"heading":"Technical Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A modern Design Researcher should combine human research + data literacy."},{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Excel/Sheets"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Miro/FigJam"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"PowerPoint/Keynote"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Qualitative analysis"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Power BI/Tableau"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Python/R"},{"text":"Basic–Intermediate"}],[{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Intermediate"}],[{"text":"AI research tools"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Presentation/storytelling"},{"text":"Advanced"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Particularly valuable combination"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design","Research","Psychology","Statistics","Data","AI"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This is much stronger than being purely visual-design oriented."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Start internships from Year 2, preferably Year 3 onward."},{"type":"h","text":"Good internship targets"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Product design companies"},{"text":"Industrial design studios"},{"text":"UX agencies"},{"text":"Consumer goods companies"},{"text":"Automotive companies"},{"text":"Electronics companies"},{"text":"FMCG companies"},{"text":"E-commerce companies"},{"text":"Technology companies"},{"text":"Research organisations"},{"text":"Innovation labs"},{"text":"Design consultancies"},{"text":"Market research companies"},{"text":"Service design firms"},{"text":"Startups"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Search titles"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Research Intern"},{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"User Research Intern"},{"text":"Product Research Intern"},{"text":"Consumer Insights Intern"},{"text":"Design Strategy Intern"},{"text":"Innovation Research Intern"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Human Factors Research Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship target"},{"type":"p","text":"Try to complete:"},{"type":"h","text":"2–3 internships + 1 live industry research project"},{"type":"p","text":"before graduation."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certificates are secondary to a strong portfolio, but selected training can help."},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Design Thinking"},{"text":"Human-Centred Design"},{"text":"User Research Methods"},{"text":"Qualitative Research"},{"text":"Quantitative Research"},{"text":"Usability Testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Power BI/Tableau"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Python/R"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Service Design"},{"text":"Product Design"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Design Strategy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Psychology"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful supplementary learning:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cognitive Psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Consumer Psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural Economics"},{"text":"Human Factors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not collect 15–20 certificates. A recruiter will usually learn more from three excellent research case studies than from a long certificate list."}]},{"heading":"Jobs You Can Actually Target","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Directly after B.Des"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Fit"],"rows":[[{"text":"Design Research Intern"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Design Research Assistant"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Junior Design Researcher"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"UX Research Associate"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"User Research Associate"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Product Research Associate"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Consumer Research Associate"},{"text":"Very Good"}],[{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Excellent"}],[{"text":"Design Strategy Associate"},{"text":"Good"}],[{"text":"Innovation Research Associate"},{"text":"Very Good"}],[{"text":"Human Factors Research Assistant"},{"text":"Good"}],[{"text":"Service Design Research Associate"},{"text":"Good"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"After 2–4 years"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Researcher"},{"text":"UX Researcher"},{"text":"Product Researcher"},{"text":"Consumer Insights Researcher"},{"text":"Service Design Researcher"},{"text":"Innovation Researcher"},{"text":"Human Factors Researcher"},{"text":"Behavioural Researcher"},{"text":"Design Strategist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"After 5–10 years"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Design Researcher"},{"text":"Lead UX Researcher"},{"text":"Senior Product Researcher"},{"text":"Research Lead"},{"text":"Design Strategy Lead"},{"text":"Research Manager"},{"text":"Head of Design Research"},{"text":"Head of User Research"}]}]},{"heading":"Employer-Ready Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest graduate profile would be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Product/Industrial Design","Human-Centred Design","UX Research","Qualitative Research","Quantitative Research","Psychology","Statistics","Figma","Excel","Power BI","SQL","AI Research Tools","Strong Portfolio"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination gives considerably more flexibility than a traditional industrial-design-only profile."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Options in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A master's degree is not mandatory for every Design Research position, but it can be valuable for advanced research, strategy and academic careers."},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant PG options"},{"type":"table","header":["PG","Suitable Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"M.Des"},{"text":"Advanced design/research"}],[{"text":"M.Des UX/HCI"},{"text":"UX & digital research"}],[{"text":"M.Des Industrial Design"},{"text":"Product/industrial research"}],[{"text":"M.Des Service Design"},{"text":"Service research"}],[{"text":"MA/MSc Psychology"},{"text":"Behavioural research"}],[{"text":"MSc Cognitive Science"},{"text":"Human cognition/behaviour"}],[{"text":"MSc Human Factors"},{"text":"Human-product interaction"}],[{"text":"MA Design Studies"},{"text":"Design research/theory"}],[{"text":"MBA Marketing"},{"text":"Consumer research"}],[{"text":"MBA Product Management"},{"text":"Product research/strategy"}],[{"text":"MSc Market Research/Consumer Insights"},{"text":"Consumer research"}],[{"text":"MA Sociology/Anthropology"},{"text":"Ethnographic research"}],[{"text":"MSc Data Analytics"},{"text":"Data-driven research"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For academic/research-intensive careers, a master's followed by research experience and potentially a PhD becomes more relevant."}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Opportunities","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After gaining experience, the career can branch into several high-value areas."},{"type":"h","text":"1. UX Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Users","Digital products","Behaviour","Usability"]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Product Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Customers","Product needs","Product decisions"]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Industrial Design Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["People","Physical products","Ergonomics","Product innovation"]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Consumer Insights"},{"type":"flow","items":["Consumers","Markets","Behaviour","Business strategy"]},{"type":"h","text":"5. Service Design Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Customers","Journeys","Service systems"]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Human Factors"},{"type":"flow","items":["Human capabilities","Product/system design","Safety/usability"]},{"type":"h","text":"7. Behavioural Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Psychology","Behaviour","Experiments","Product/business decisions"]},{"type":"h","text":"8. Design Strategy"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Opportunities","Business/product strategy"]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful international fields include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Research"},{"text":"Industrial Design"},{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Service Design"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"Design Strategy"},{"text":"Behavioural Science"},{"text":"Consumer Research"},{"text":"Innovation Management"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Countries commonly considered include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Denmark"},{"text":"Finland"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Italy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For international study, evaluate programmes based on research labs, industry projects, faculty, portfolio requirements and graduate employment, rather than selecting a programme only because it contains “Design” in its name."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Product / Industrial Design","Design Research Intern","Research Assistant / UX Research Associate","Junior Design Researcher","Design Researcher","Senior Design Researcher","Lead Design Researcher","Research Manager / Design Strategy Lead","Head of Design Research"]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible lateral paths:"},{"type":"p","text":"Design Research"},{"type":"p","text":"├── UX Research"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Product Research"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Consumer Insights"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Service Design"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Human Factors"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Behavioural Research"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Innovation Strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Product Strategy"}]},{"heading":"AI and the Future of Design Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will change the workflow substantially, but it is unlikely to eliminate the need for high-quality human research."},{"type":"h","text":"AI can assist with"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Interview summarisation"},{"text":"Research-note organisation"},{"text":"Qualitative coding"},{"text":"Pattern discovery"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Competitor analysis"},{"text":"Trend detection"},{"text":"Persona drafts"},{"text":"Research repository search"},{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Synthetic research hypotheses"},{"text":"Prototype feedback analysis"},{"text":"Sentiment analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human researchers remain responsible for"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Selecting appropriate research methods"},{"text":"Recruiting appropriate participants"},{"text":"Asking high-quality questions"},{"text":"Understanding context"},{"text":"Detecting research bias"},{"text":"Validating evidence"},{"text":"Interpreting ambiguous behaviour"},{"text":"Ethical research"},{"text":"Protecting participant privacy"},{"text":"Making strategic recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2030–2045 opportunity"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest researchers will increasingly work as:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Human Insight","Behavioural Science","Data","AI","Product Strategy"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Newer roles may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI Product Researcher"},{"text":"Human-AI Interaction Researcher"},{"text":"AI Experience Researcher"},{"text":"Behavioural AI Researcher"},{"text":"AI Product Strategy Researcher"},{"text":"Research Operations Specialist"},{"text":"Research Intelligence Lead"},{"text":"Human Factors & AI Researcher"}]}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Des Product/Industrial Design"},{"text":"Design thinking"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Product fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Contextual inquiry"},{"text":"Qualitative analysis"},{"text":"Quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Ethnographic research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Behaviour"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Cognitive behaviour"},{"text":"Consumer behaviour"},{"text":"Human factors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Miro/FigJam"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Basic Python/R"},{"text":"AI research tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"4–6 strong research case studies"},{"text":"2–3 real-world research projects"},{"text":"1 quantitative research project"},{"text":"1 ethnographic/contextual study"},{"text":"1 usability study"},{"text":"1 product innovation study"},{"text":"1 internship or live industry project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research presentation"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Report writing"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"},{"text":"Critical thinking"},{"text":"Evidence-based decision-making"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Practical Path"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Product/Industrial Design","Learn human-centred design + psychology + research methods","Master interviews, observation, surveys and usability testing","Learn Figma + Excel + statistics + Power BI","Add SQL + basic Python/R + AI-assisted research","Complete 4–6 high-quality research case studies","Do 2–3 internships/live projects","Enter as Design Research Assistant / UX Research Associate / Product Research Associate","Move into Design Researcher / UX Researcher / Product Researcher","Specialise in Product, UX, Service, Consumer, Behavioural or Human Factors Research","Progress toward Senior Researcher → Research Lead → Research Manager / Head of Design Research"]},{"type":"note","label":"Overall assessment","text":"Excellent career alignment. B.Des Product/Industrial Design provides a particularly strong foundation because the student already understands products and design; adding research methodology, psychology, statistics, data analytics and AI transforms that foundation into a highly employable modern Design Research profile."}]}]}